&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the direction for the AI Platforms team, with a clear roadmap that balances today&#39;s internal needs with where the product is going&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and scale the team to full capacity by strategically hiring and continuing to develop current team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve the shared AI platform: model access and routing, agent runtime, MCP integrations, evals, agent identity, and cost controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own our AI end-user platforms, enabling a multiplayer ecosystem working side by side with agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with core teams to evolve our Agentic PDLC, including the tools, environments, review practices, and workflows through which AI agents help plan, write, test, review, and ship code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend the platform from internal productivity to the product, defining how product teams access, run, and monitor AI inference and AI-powered features in production at member scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption by making the right way the easy way: paved paths, reusable skills and components, champions, and enablement that engineers choose to use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security, Privacy, and Legal to build data handling, auditability, and safeguards into the platform from day one, with the trust our members expect from a family safety company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and report outcomes that matter, such as adoption, quality, cost per outcome, and time to ship, rather than usage counts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to the work: review designs, unblock teams, and make build-versus-buy calls as the model and tooling landscape change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience leading engineering teams that build platforms or infrastructure used by other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating production AI systems, such as agentic workflows, large language model (LLM) integrations, retrieval, and evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of MCP and agent orchestration, including how agents connect to internal systems with appropriate controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI inference in production, including serving, latency, reliability, provider management, and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving the adoption of new engineering practices across a large engineering organization through influence, without becoming the bottleneck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on technical judgment: comfortable reviewing architecture, setting technical direction, and staying close to implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working where the platform, the operating model, and the product use cases are all taking shape at once, and a clear communicator with both executives and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: experience with consumer-scale mobile products or privacy-sensitive data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
