&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the decision scientists and data scientists on the team, and set the quality bar for both disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the MAU driver model and the forecast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the exploratory work that drives the strategy to grow MAU.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish how an analysis gets scoped, run, reviewed, and written up, so its quality does not depend on who picked up the request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with your Revenue counterpart and Data Engineering leadership to define common metrics, align on experimentation standards, and introduce unified operating practices across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the operating model that gets the team into the roadmap conversation early, with a view on what to build and what to test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use agents and automated analysis daily, and expect the same of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape how the team works AI-native: what gets delegated to agents, what gets automated, and what stays human judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Experience &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in analytics, data science, or decision science, including 5+ years in people management in a senior leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in inferential and causal analytics. Able to lead ML practitioners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of engagement, retention, churn, and cohort metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience forecasting a company-level metric and being held to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL, plus Python or R.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Databricks, third party experimentation tools (e.g. Statsig), Tableau or similar BI tools, and AI native BI tools (e.g. Hex, AI/BI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on with coding agents (Claude Code or equivalent) in your own analytical work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with experiment design to identify and control for network effects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree or PhD with an emphasis in social science, psychology or other behavioral science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team that reports to you but sits embedded with product and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a B2C subscription business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have moved an analytics team from reactive to embedded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You coach and develop people, and you have grown analysts into leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On your teams, analysis starts from a hypothesis rather than a data request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built the standards a team works from, and got people to use them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are curious about why people behave the way they do, not just what they did.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You decide what the team does not work on, and you can defend it.&lt;/li&gt;
