&lt;h3&gt;About The Team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on the Verticals team within Life360 — the group building the next frontier of meaningful connection beyond the core family circle. This role&#39;s initial focus is Aging in Place: helping aging parents stay safely independent while giving the families around them real peace of mind. Over time, this role may flex to support other emerging verticals — Things (Tile, connected trackers) or Pets — as priorities shift, so we&#39;re looking for someone who wants to help define the pattern for new member segments, not just ship one feature set.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a product-minded, AI-Native engineering team. That means AI isn&#39;t just a tool we use — it&#39;s how we work. We&#39;ve redesigned our team workflows around AI, treating it as a first-class collaborator at every stage: ideation, coding, testing, review, and iteration. We ship faster and go deeper because of it, and we&#39;re looking for someone who wants to help define what that looks like at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life360 is hiring an AI-Native Engineer — a senior engineer who doesn&#39;t just use AI tools, but thinks natively in them. You&#39;ll be central to how the Verticals team builds products, where AI has reshaped how the entire team designs, builds, and ships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll design and build features that serve one of our most important and fastest-growing member segments: aging parents who want to stay safely connected with, and independent from, the families who care about them. As the priorities change, you may also apply these same patterns to Things (connected trackers) or Pets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll build and evolve our modern AI-Native engineering workflows — from how we write code, to how we run standups, to how we think about team velocity. You&#39;ll evolve the standard others follow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will take full ownership of what you build from the first line of code through production, on-call, and the member impact it has.&amp;nbsp; You are someone who obsesses over the humans on the other end of the product, not just the ticket.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full-stack experience is strongly preferred for this role — you should be comfortable moving between backend services and the mobile surfaces that expose them. Our stack spans Spring Boot microservices, Java, Kafka, and Kafka Streams on the backend, a modern cloud-native platform on AWS, and native iOS (Swift) and Android (Kotlin) apps on the client side.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year, success looks like having shipped end-to-end features serving the Aging in Place member segment and establishing at least one AI-native workflow the broader team adopts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For candidates based in the US, the salary range for this position is $118,500 to $216,500 USD. For candidates based out of Canada, the salary range for this position is &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;$171,500 to $201,000&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;CAD. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: Please be aware that the job title for positions in Canada will be &quot;Developer&quot; in lieu of &quot;Engineer.&quot; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;We take into consideration an individual&#39;s background, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience in determining final salary. Base pay may also vary based on geographic location, with US work locations falling into one of three geographic tiers.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Total compensation is inclusive of equity compensation in the form of &lt;strong&gt;Restricted Stock Units (RSUs)&lt;/strong&gt;, as well as a comprehensive benefits package, including medical, dental, vision, financial, and other benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship end-to-end across the stack — from backend services and APIs through to the iOS and Android surfaces members actually use — moving fluidly between layers as the feature demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with AI (Claude Code) as a first-class collaborator — your primary workflow involves orchestrating agents to create specs, generate results, and perform reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define and codify AI-Native engineering practices for the Verticals team, establishing playbooks the broader org can adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build across the full stack as needed — shipping polished, performant, and reliable experiences to tens of millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with product managers and designers to turn complex user problems into elegant, scalable engineering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architectural decisions, code reviews, and a culture of craft and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
