&lt;h3&gt;About Life360&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life360’s mission is to keep people close to the ones they love. Our category-leading mobile app, Tile tracking devices, and Pet GPS tracker empower members to protect the people, pets, and things they care about most with a range of services, including location sharing, safe driver reports, and crash detection with emergency dispatch. Life360 serves approximately 102.4 million monthly active users (MAU), as of June 30, 2026, across more than 180 countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life360 delivers peace of mind and enhances everyday family life with seamless coordination for all the moments that matter, big and small. By continuing to innovate and deliver for our customers, we have become a household name and the must-have mobile-based membership for families (and those friends who are basically family).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life360 has more than 500 (and growing!) remote-first employees. For more information, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://life360.com/&quot;&gt;life360.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Life360 is a remote First company, which means a remote work environment will be the primary experience for all employees. All positions, unless otherwise specified, can be performed remotely (within the US and Canada) regardless of any specified location above.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;We are AI Native&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an AI native company where AI is an integral part of how we build and operate. AI tool usage during interviews varies by role. You may be asked to demonstrate proficiency with AI tools, discuss how you leverage AI, or complete interview exercises without AI assistance. Your Recruiter will provide clear guidance as you move through the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Undisclosed use of AI not previously discussed with or approved by your Recruiter may impact your candidacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue Experiences team (Direct Revenue org) owns the premium experience behind Life360 membership. We work on subscription tiering, pricing, packaging, and positioning, and we own the premium features and services members pay for: the ones that exist today and the ones we haven&#39;t built yet. This includes maintaining these services and ensuring they consistently meet the highest quality standards for our premium users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our focal point is ownership and quality. We extend the premium feature set by building new features while keeping the existing ones healthy, fast, and worth the price. We still run experiments across paywalls, pricing, ad placement and mediation because every monetization and packaging decision should be grounded in evidence, not instinct. But experiments are how we decide what to build and how to package it, not the whole job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a product-minded, AI-Native engineering team. AI isn&#39;t just a tool we use — it&#39;s how we work. We treat it as a first-class collaborator at every stage: ideation, coding, testing, review, and iteration. We ship faster and go deeper because of it, and we&#39;re looking for someone who wants to help define what that looks like at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Life360 is hiring an AI-Native Senior Software Engineer II — a builder who thinks natively in AI tooling and takes real ownership of outcomes, not just tickets. You&#39;ll be central to how the Revenue Experiences team builds, ships, and maintains the premium features and monetization surfaces behind Life360 membership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll take ideas from a brief to a shipped product that holds up for 100M+ monthly active users, and you&#39;ll own premium features end-to-end: building new ones and keeping existing ones reliable and good as they grow. Why now: premium features are what members pay for and the set keeps growing, so the quality bar rises with every launch. This role keeps the existing features strong while we build the new ones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year, success looks like owning the end-to-end delivery of several features or experiments that contribute to global revenue growth or improve the quality of premium features we already serve to our existing customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For candidates based in the US, the salary range for this position is $118,500 to $216,500 USD. For candidates based out of Canada, the salary range for this position is 171,500 to 201,000 CAD.&lt;/em&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: Please be aware that the job title for positions in Canada will be &quot;Developer&quot; in lieu of &quot;Engineer.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;We take into consideration an individual&#39;s background, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience in determining final salary. Base pay may also vary based on geographic location, with US work locations falling into one of three geographic tiers.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Total compensation is inclusive of equity compensation in the form of &lt;strong&gt;Restricted Stock Units (RSUs)&lt;/strong&gt;, as well as a comprehensive benefits package, including medical, dental, vision, financial, and other benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
