&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Taste and craft&lt;/strong&gt; — You have opinions about what a good experiment, a good rollout, and a good user experience look like, and you can articulate why — not just execute a spec.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth mindset&lt;/strong&gt; — You structure problems precisely, learn quickly, show interest outside &quot;your lane,&quot; and are always happy to try something new.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-native working style&lt;/strong&gt; — You use AI tooling (Claude Code or equivalent) as a genuine development partner: delegating discrete tasks, reviewing outputs critically, and running parallel workstreams rather than hand-holding one agent at a time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative approach&lt;/strong&gt; — You communicate clearly, work well across teams, and value diverse perspectives; you give and take feedback well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We believe value alignment and problem-solving ability matter more than checking every technical box. We&#39;re happy to help you grow into areas where you have less experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with an experimentation platform (Statsig, LaunchDarkly, Optimizely, Eppo, GrowthBook, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in mobile analytics pipelines (Amplitude, Segment, Snowflake/Databricks downstream).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Bayesian or sequential testing methods and how they affect client-side implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous work on subscription, paywall, pricing, or onboarding surfaces at consumer scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep in at least one of Kotlin/Android, Swift, or React, and comfortable shipping in another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to mobile open source or internal developer tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
