&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daily use&lt;/strong&gt; — You use AI coding assistants (we support Claude Code, Cursor, and GitHub Copilot) for real, substantive tasks: analysis, coding, refactoring, testing, navigating codebases, and documentation, not just research or autocomplete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Judgment and ownership&lt;/strong&gt; — AI-generated code gets the same review you&#39;d give any PR. You are accountable for everything you ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Velocity&lt;/strong&gt; — We expect senior engineers who use AI well to operate with meaningful leverage, taking on problems that would otherwise require a larger team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team leadership&lt;/strong&gt; — You share what works, automate prompting strategies others can build on, and help teammates earlier in their AI workflow adoption get up to speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous learning&lt;/strong&gt; — The tooling changes fast. You stay current and bring recommendations to the team when something would meaningfully improve how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
